@startuml 08-deployment
title Deployment diagram - docker compose up --build
skinparam shadowing false

node "Developer computer" {
  node "Browser" as Browser {
    artifact "React app\n(access token in memory,\nrefresh token in HttpOnly cookie)" as App
  }
  artifact "CLI client\n(npm run demo:cli, X-API-Key)" as CLI

  node "Docker (network metering 172.30.0.0/24)" as Docker {
    node "web\nnginx 1.27\n172.30.0.10" as Web {
      artifact "static build\n+ /api/* proxy\n+ CSP & security headers" as WebArt
    }
    node "api\nNode 22, Fastify" as Api {
      artifact "dist/server.js\nmigrations + seed at start" as ApiArt
    }
    node "postgres\nPostgreSQL 17" as Pg {
      database "metering" as Db
    }
    storage "volume pgdata" as Vol
  }
}

cloud "OpenAI / OpenRouter\n(optional, AI_PROVIDER=openai)" as LLM

Browser --> Web : http://localhost:8080\n(127.0.0.1 / ::1 only)
Web --> Api : /api/* -> http://api:3000\nX-Forwarded-For (trusted from web only)
CLI --> Api : http://localhost:3000/api/v1
Api --> Pg : postgres://...:5432\npool (DATABASE_POOL_MAX)
Pg --> Vol : data survives restarts
Api ..> LLM : HTTPS (only when enabled)

note bottom of Docker
  restart: unless-stopped on every service
  postgres healthy (pg_isready over TCP) -> api healthy (/ready) -> web
  ports published on loopback only: 8080 (web), 3000 (API, Swagger), 5433 (psql)
end note
@enduml
